---
title = "Parse RFC 3339 and ISO 8601 timestamps"
meta_title = "How to parse RFC 3339 and ISO 8601 timestamps"
subtitle = "using the Gleam time package"
description = "The Gleam time package provides time functionality that works with Gleam on both Erlang and JavaScript"
tags = ["time"]
---

Timestamp strings like `2026-09-06T17:00:09.398Z` match the format specified in
[RFC 3339](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3339#section-5.6).

The `gleam_time` package has a function for parsing these timestamps on both
the Erlang and JavaScript targets. Add it as a dependency to your package:

```cli
gleam add gleam_time
```

Use the [`timestamp.parse_rfc3339`](https://gleam-time.hexdocs.pm/gleam/time/timestamp.html#parse_rfc3339)
function to parse the timestamp.

```gleam
import gleam/time/timestamp.{type Timestamp}

pub fn time() -> Result(Timestamp, Nil) {
  timestamp.parse_rfc3339("2026-09-06T17:00:09.398Z")
}
```

::: alert-warning
### Other ISO 8601 formats

ISO 8601 specifies other formats such as `2026-249` and `2026-W37-7`. These are
not valid RFC 3339 timestamps, so if you need to parse them you may want to use
the [`datetime_iso8601`](https://datetime-iso8601.hexdocs.pm/) package instead.

:::
